cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Prime Number Studies: independent re-derivations, measurements
  and negative results around the division table
message: >-
  If you use this material, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Osman
    family-names: ""
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Osman209/prime-number-studies'
abstract: >-
  Notes, measurements and verified code from a self-directed study
  of the multiplicative structure of the integers, starting from the
  division table. Contains independent re-derivations of known
  results (the sieve of Sundaram; the Hardy-Littlewood singular
  series; the explicit formula), documented negative results and
  controls, and runnable verification scripts for every table and
  figure. No claim is made about the Riemann Hypothesis.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - prime numbers
  - sieve of Sundaram
  - divisor function
  - Hardy-Littlewood singular series
  - Riemann zeta function
  - reproducible research
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.1.0
date-released: '2026-07-28'
